### npm init-y
for a project when u make the folder and then do npm init -y, it creates the package.json for it.
package.json is basically the metadata/configuration file for a Node project.

### what's express?? and need? 
while routing so many if else condns for what to do for each route so we use a framework on top of node.js
node.js provides a runtime environment for us to run js outside of our browser. 
express is a framework on top of node.js which makes it easier to create http servers and apis.


### JSON data:
APIs normally communicate using JSON, rather than returning HTML/text pages.

Eventually QueueFlow might return:
{ \
  "queueId": 12, \
  "name": "Mess Counter", \
  "position": 7, \
  "status": "waiting" \
}
The frontend can then take this data and display it however it wants.
That's the fundamental idea behind a REST API.

### HTTP methods:
GET → read
